RF.put("questb:b60",{"8700":{"id":8700,"t":"Band of Unending Life","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Magisterial Ring, 2 Alabaster Idols, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Magisterial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Alabaster Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, fellow/sister druid.","rew":"You will receive:\nBand of Unending Life\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gems on the ring for you. You'll find the finished piece is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"1020":{"id":1020,"t":"Orendil's Cure","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Orendil's Cure to Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar.\nOrendil's Cure\nProvided: Orendil's Cure","desc":"‹name›, I have created a cure that I believe will help the afflicted child. Take it to Astranaar and give it to the child's parent, Pelturas Whitemoon.\nTo reach Astranaar, follow the road south, then east.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I must apologize, for I have no time to speak. My child, Relara, is deathly ill!","done":"This is from Orendil?\nHis skill with herbs and healing is great. This cure gives me hope, when before I had little...","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.4,"y":38.6,"n":"Orendil Broadleaf","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":37.4,"y":51.8,"n":"Pelturas Whitemoon","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1420":{"id":1420,"t":"Report to Helgrum","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Neeka's Report to Helgrum the Swift in Stonard.\nNeeka's Report\nProvided: Neeka's Report","desc":"I wrote a fresh report for Helgrum in Stonard. Bring it to him.\nAnd if you consider yourself an outrunner, then don't lose your way. Or fall to an enemy.","rew":"Experience: 2,350\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You returned. You have a report?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. From Neeka's report, I see the Alliance is not without its own problems. And we may find that some enemies are shared between us.\nBadlands Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":6.5,"y":47.2,"n":"Neeka Bloodscar","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.7,"y":55.2,"n":"Helgrum the Swift","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97900":{"id":97900,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Dwukk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":40.6,"n":"Dwukk","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94300":{"id":94300,"t":"Craftsmans writ big voodoo mask","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Big Voodoo Mask\nBig Voodoo Mask","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Big Voodoo Mask, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Big Voodoo Mask Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94300","cats":["crafting"]},"94220":{"id":94220,"t":"Craftsmans writ pearl handled dagger","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Pearl-Handled Dagger\nPearl-handled Dagger","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Pearl-Handled Dagger, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"It is unwise to sneak up on me, ‹race›. Speak quickly, and speak quietly.","done":"Oh, you are delivering my dagger? Hah, I suppose my threat rang quite hollow then, hm?\nI must stay on high alert given my duties here, and especially with oth-- ahem, the foul Syndicate roaming about elsewhere here.\nWould you be so kind as to part with the blade, now? I must get back to my task.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":30.4,"y":61.2,"n":"Alan Sneeks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7900":{"id":7900,"t":"Torn Bear Pelts","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Torn Bear Pelt Giant Ashenvale Bear 30.3 % , Ursol'lok 23.3 % , Elder Ashenvale Bear 19.4 % , Elder Gray Bear 18.5 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n4 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Children love toys! And no matter what race, I've found that all children love furry, plushy toys made from torn bear pelts!\nYou can get those pelts from the bears of Ashenvale or Hillsbrad. Bring me a heap of them and earn yourself a heap of Darkmoon Faire tickets!","done":"Nice pelts, ‹name›! I'll get someone to sew these into a bunch of plush toys. With a little stuffing and some paint, I think they'll be the envy of children across Azeroth!\nTickets? Ah yes, your payment!\nHere they are!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7500":{"id":7500,"t":"The Arcanist's Cookbook","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nThe Arcanist's Cookbook A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: The Arcanist's Cookbook","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: The Arcanist's Cookbook End Lorekeeper Kildrath Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Mage Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7500","cats":["dire-maul"]},"1260":{"id":1260,"t":"Morgan Stern","lv":38,"min":33,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Morgan Stern in Theramore.","desc":"I'm developing a new menu for the restaurant. It will be filled with rural dishes with a \"bayou\" theme. I think my clientele at the Blue Recluse will love them!\nI sent my nephew Morgan to Theramore, a city on the edge of the Dustwallow Marsh. He's there gathering recipes from the locals, and I must know what he found so far.\nThe trip to Theramore is long. Too long for me. But I bet a young ‹class› like yourself would jump at the chance to travel, yes?","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Oh, my uncle sent you, did he?\nWell I've been researching recipes and I have some leads, but I need help.\nHelp from someone willing to get his feet wet.\nStormwind City Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":93.6,"n":"Angus Stern","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.3,"y":45.5,"n":"Morgan Stern","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"60":{"id":60,"t":"Kobold Candles","lv":7,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Large Candles to William Pestle in Goldshire.\n8 Large Candle Kobold Geomancer 66 % , Kobold Tunneler 66 % , Goldtooth 66 % , Kobold Miner 66 %","desc":"Hello, good sir/my lady! Do you have a moment?\nMy brother and I run an apothecary in Stormwind, and I'm here to gather large candles for their wax. Can you help me?\nYou can get large candles from kobolds, and I hear rumors that kobolds are infesting the Elwynn mines ... the Fargodeep mine to the south and Jasperlode Mine to the east. I suggest looking for candles in one of those places.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Glowing Wax Stick\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 480\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you gather those candles yet?","done":"You were busy hunting kobolds, were you? Thanks for the candles, ‹name›, and here's your reward...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"William Pestle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91740":{"id":91740,"t":"Croakys head","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Croaky's Head to Merell Ross at Ridgepoint Tower.\nProvided: Croaky's Head","desc":"This murloc has no doubt been terrorizing the local roads for some time. You suspect the nearby watch guards will want to know of its demise.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes?","done":"We lost two members of the watch last week to the murlocs, ‹class›. Hopefully with their leader slain, we can start pushing them out of Elwynn.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.6,"y":79.2,"n":"Merell Ross","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"8460":{"id":8460,"t":"Timbermaw Ally","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grazle wants you to prove yourself by killing 6 Deadwood Warriors, 6 Deadwood Pathfinders, and 6 Deadwood Gardeners. Return to him in southern Felwood near the Emerald Sanctuary when you are done.\nDeadwood Warrior slain : 0/ 6\nDeadwood Pathfinder slain : 0/ 6\nDeadwood Gardener slain : 0/ 6","desc":"The Timbermaw are the only furbolg tribe to escape the corruption. However, many other races kill furbolg blindly now, without bothering to see if they are friend or foe. For this reason, the Timbermaw furbolg trust very few.\nAre you interested in proving yourself? Drive back the corrupted Deadwood tribe of Felwood and we may one day consider you an ally. You'll find the first Deadwood tribe - warriors, pathfinders and gardeners - to my west.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEarth Warder's Vest Belt of the Den Watcher\nExperience: 4,400\n+150 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"Keep at it, ‹name›. If you are to earn our trust, you will need to prove yourself to us.","done":"We suffer much from the events of the past. Thank you for what you have done to help protect the Timbermaw. As a sign of our growing friendship, please accept this humble offering.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.9,"y":85,"n":"Grazle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2940":{"id":2940,"t":"Feralas: A History","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ask Daryn Lightwind if you may borrow her book.","desc":"This book looks as if no one has opened it for quite a long time. Its covers are quite worn, and its pages yellowed, but after examining it, you notice that it might be just what Troyas is looking for.\nYou pick it up, but realize you should probably ask before borrowing it.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"So, you'd like to borrow Feralas: A History?\nLet me think...\nI will allow you to borrow this book, ‹name›, but only if you do something for me first.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.2,"y":91.5,"n":"Feralas: A History","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":92.2,"n":"Daryn Lightwind","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"1580":{"id":1580,"t":"Electropellers","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Electropellers to Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.\n12 Electropeller","desc":"We know you're lucky, but... just how lucky are you, ‹name›?\nOne night I was wandering the roads of Darkshore. I was looking for a good river or lake to try my new self-propelled, exploding duck decoy and I think I was a little tipsy... because I passed out and awoke hours later in Auberdine. My hair was singed and my bag of electropellers was gone! I must have dropped them in the water!\nI need those electropellers! Maybe you can fish them out of some lake or stream in Darkshore...","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Aquadynamic Fish Lens\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Did you find any electropellers? I'll need them if I'm to continue my research on duck decoys...","done":"I can't believe it! You found them! You are the best fisherman I've ever seen!\nThank you, ‹name›. And here, take these. Although you're so good and you probably don't need them, they will help you with your fishing.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37,"y":44.1,"n":"Wizbang Cranktoggle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"9260":{"id":9260,"t":"Investigate the Scourge of Stormwind","lv":6,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 410 experience instead of 400, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Stormwind and investigate the glowing runic circles near their encampment.\n3 Dim Necrotic Stone Skeletal Soldier 35 % , Spectral Apparition 35 % , Spectral Spirit 31 % , Skeletal Trooper 31 %","desc":"The Lich King has sent his undead upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Stormwind from these accursed invaders?\nThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you. Go!","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410","back":"Have you investigated the invasion yet? There's no time for dawdling!","done":"Hmm. From what you've told me, the voices within the circles... they must be used for communication of some kind. I shudder to think what unnatural minds are contacted through such magic. Regardless, you seem to have emerged whole and sane. The Argent Dawn appreciates your service.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest Tirisfal Glades Dun Morogh Mulgore Durotar Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69,"y":82.8,"n":"Lieutenant Orrin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"700":{"id":700,"t":"A King's Tribute","lv":31,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to King Magni Bronzebeard.","desc":"Ah, such fine stone comes from Lordaeron. Such a shame the land is in such shambles.\nBut the Memorial came out quite well! I should think the King will be most pleased with it.\nNow if you will, please send word to His Majesty that the Memorial is complete as requested.","rew":"You will receive:\nIronforge Memorial Ring\nExperience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"The granite seems but a small token compared to a great dwarf's life. But no dwarf shall last on this planet for eternity.\nLet us just hope that the memorial stands as a reminder to those who will trod the great Azeroth of the future. Lest we not forget it is for them that brave soldiers such as Sully Balloo so valiantly gave their lives.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.3,"y":35.2,"n":"Grand Mason Marblesten","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"98300":{"id":98300,"t":"Word to ironforge","lv":34,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Howin's Missive to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.\nProvided: Howin's Missive","desc":"My work here is far from over, ‹name›. And I need tae send word to me wife Claira in Aerie Peak--and get Falstad an update as well.\nBut that's my business. Wildhammer business.\nThat said, you ought tae let King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge know about all this as well. Wetlands is but a stone's throw from his lands, and none of what's happenin' here is good news on one's doorstep. This letter oughta do the trick.\nYe can travel back through Dun Algaz or fly from Menethil Harbor to get to Ironforge.","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+10 reputation with Ironforge\nWetlands Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.4,"y":42,"n":"Howin Kindfeather","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":39.4,"y":55.8,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2860":{"id":2860,"t":"Master of the Wild Leather","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Jangdor's Letter to Una, the master leatherworker of Thunder Bluff.\nJangdor's Letter\nProvided: Jangdor's Letter","desc":"‹name›, you have learned all I am able to teach you. There is, however, one remaining pattern for Wild Leather armor. I will not require you to toil needlessly for this; you've earned it outright, and then some. This pattern, however, is one that I cannot freely share with you.\nMy teacher, the one who brought me into the craft, is the one who must reward you. Take this note to Una; she teaches leatherworking in Thunder Bluff. Show her the letter, and let her acknowledge you as an equal, as I do.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Cloak\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Greetings, ‹race›... from your countenance I can tell you are a leatherworker as am I. Have you come to draw from my skills, or perhaps you have other business with me?","done":"Ah yes, Jangdor sent you. I am pleased to see that one of my finest students now has a student of his own.\nHis dedication and his talents with leather are impressive. For him to compliment you so in this letter, it is a sign of respect I acknowledge.\nI am aware that he has taught you the art of Wild Leather. Allow me to finish your training with this pattern. Make good use of it; few in the world know the secrets of Wild Leather cloaks.\nFeralas Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":41.5,"y":42.6,"n":"Una","e":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"780":{"id":780,"t":"The Battleboars","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to kill Battleboars and bring back 8 Battleboar Snouts and 8 Battleboar Flanks.\n8 Battleboar Snout Battleboar 80 % , Bristleback Battleboar 80 %\n8 Battleboar Flank Battleboar 80 % , Bristleback Battleboar 80 %","desc":"The Battleboars of Brambleblade Ravine to the east are encroaching on our tribal hunting grounds. They are trained to be malicious by the Bristleback Quilboars with whom we are at war.\nGo and slay the vile creatures and bring back some snouts and flanks so that we can make stew for our young.","rew":"You will receive:\nNomadic Vest 10 Tough Hunk of Bread\nExperience: 450\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The aggression of the Battleboars is increasing. Have you sent them a clear message and brought back some snouts and flanks yet?","done":"Most excellent. These ingredients will make a fine stew and the loss of those boars should be a fair lesson to those vile Bristlebacks.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9100":{"id":9100,"t":"Frostfire Gloves","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Frostfire Gloves if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Gloves, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps and 4 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Gloves\n8 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Gloves\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Gloves.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"7660":{"id":7660,"t":"Wolf Swapping - Arctic Wolf","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horn of the Arctic Wolf","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHorn of the Swift Brown Wolf Horn of the Swift Gray Wolf Horn of the Swift Timber Wolf","back":"If you bring me your old fast wolf, I will trade it in for one from the new pack. The new wolf will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift wolves we already have around the yard here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":69.4,"y":12.2,"n":"Ogunaro Wolfrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"4300":{"id":4300,"t":"Bone-Bladed Weapons","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 White Ravasaur Claws to Jes'rimon in Orgrimmar.\n8 White Ravasaur Claw Ravasaur Matriarch 20 % , Ravasaur 20 % , Ravasaur Runner 20 % , Ravasaur Hunter 20 % and 3 more","desc":"Hmm, maybe there be somethin' you can do for the Hand now that me think 'bout it. Yes, Jes'rimon could use your help for sure.\nIn Un'Goro Crater there be raptors with deadly claws. Some of those raptors sometimes have white claws instead of ones black like death. The Hand have... clients... that like weapons crafted from these claws. Bring me many of those white claws, and me pay you good coin. Do it fast enough, and maybe me help you in other ways.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWhite Bone Band White Bone Shredder White Bone Spear\nMoney: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Me clients are not so patient, ‹name›. Have you gotten any of the claws yet?","done":"Ah, these do nicely. Thank you, ‹name›. An' you be here long before they needed... that be good.\nMaybe we have a weapon fashioned for you from the claws. What do you say?\nOrgrimmar Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.5,"y":34.1,"n":"Jes'rimon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9020":{"id":9020,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Shadowcraft Boots, Shadowcraft Pants and Shadowcraft Spaulders.\nShadowcraft Boots Rattlegore 16 % in Scholomance\nShadowcraft Pants Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nShadowcraft Spaulders Cannon Master Willey 0 % in Stratholme\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Boots Darkmantle Pants Darkmantle Spaulders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8940":{"id":8940,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Devout Belt and a set of Devout Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nDevout Belt Blackhand Summoner 7.6 % , Smolderthorn Shadow Priest 4.4 % , Firebrand Dreadweaver 4.3 % , Scarshield Spellbinder 2 % and 2 more\nDevout Gloves Archivist Galford 0 % in Stratholme","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Belt Virtuous Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5660":{"id":5660,"t":"Touch of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"You be far from home, ‹class›. You be needed there, back in your city under the ground. Your mistress, the one you be callin' Aelthalyste be needin' you back there. Like my tribe, there things you must learn only from her. Don't be stayin' here too long. You should be headin' to the War Quarter as fast as a zeppelin can carry you.","rew":"You will learn: Touch of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"Ah, good, another has arrived. Time may not matter to me, but to you it is of the essence. There is much for you to learn and there is much I wish to teach you. You simply must prove your worth. Do that, and you shall be greatly rewarded.\nDurotar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.3,"y":42.9,"n":"Tai'jin","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"2300":{"id":2300,"t":"SI:7","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stormwind and seek out Renzik \"The Shiv.\"","desc":"Renzik was looking for you, fish.\nI wouldn't keep Mathias's second in command waiting if I were you.","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"Are you ready to get to work or do you need to take a nap before we get started?\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.9,"y":65.9,"n":"Keryn Sylvius","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":71.1,"n":"Renzik \"The Shiv\"","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2380":{"id":2380,"t":"To Orgrimmar!","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shenthul at the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.","desc":"A master of stealth and deception you are not, however, all of that can and will change. You've obviously impressed those in charge with your meager skills, as the great Shenthul has asked for you by name.\nTake the road north of here to Orgrimmar and speak with Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow.","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"It is important that the Shattered Hand remains vigilant in the face of the changes Thrall wishes to bring about to the Horde. Our numbers alone will not be enough to overcome his rule - stealth and deception must be mastered.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":43.7,"n":"Kaplak","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2460":{"id":2460,"t":"The Shattered Salute","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Perform the Shattered Salute on Shenthul.","desc":"As a rogue of the Shattered Hand, it is imperative that you learn the Shattered Salute. It is the only way to truly identify another member of the Hand.\nWatch, learn, repeat.","rew":"Experience: 160","done":"Well done, ‹name›. You are now ready to proceed.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8860":{"id":8860,"t":"New Year Celebrations!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 70. Requires level 1 instead of 60. Pays 9s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring the Smokywood Supplies to Innkeeper Allison in Stormwind.\nSmokywood Supplies\nProvided: Smokywood Supplies","desc":"Stormwind is holding a celebration for the new year! All day long today you can get free booze, and at night they'll put on a firework show! It should be pretty nice... but Booty Bay is also having a party today; I bet it'll be even better!\nWell anyway, Innkeeper Allison in Stormwind needs a supply of Smoky Wood Pasture fare to help feed all the party goers. Can you do me a favor and deliver it!\nThanks, ‹name›! Innkeeper Allison is in the Gilded Rose, in the Trade District of Stormwind.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Greetings! Are you here for the party! Or perhaps you just need to rest those weary feet of yours...","done":"Oh, my Smokywood supplies! Splendid! I'll need these to feed all the people in town for the celebration!\nThank you, ‹name›. Please take this as payment, and don't forget to drink and dance with the revelers outside!\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.9,"y":71.4,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":75.3,"n":"Innkeeper Allison","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":53.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.5,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"220":{"id":220,"t":"Call of Water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\nVial of Purest Water\nProvided: Vial of Purest Water","desc":"Islen will have one more task for you before rewarding you with your next totem. The vial of water I've given you is necessary for whatever that task is.\nGo now and find her. We shall meet again some day.","rew":"You will receive:\nWater Sapta\nExperience: 460","back":"Hello again, ‹name›. You're looking well.\nWhat brings you back to me so soon?","done":"Ah, a vial of water created and blessed by Brine, and gathered by you, no less.\nThe liquid in this vial will be key in creating a sapta for you, but also used in one other task.\nThe sapta I create for you should be used to see the water spirits at the shrine in Silverpine Forest, south of the Undercity. The remaining drops, well, the remaining drops I will tell you about if you feel you are ready.\nAre you prepared for one more journey, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.4,"y":77.4,"n":"Brine","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8380":{"id":8380,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Legguards Wastewalker's Gauntlets\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8780":{"id":8780,"t":"Armor Kits for the Field","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Rugged Armor Kits and 8 Heavy Armor Kits to Janela Stouthammer at the Ironforge Brigade Outpost near Hive'Zora in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.\n8 Rugged Armor Kit Larion 10 % , Rabid Blisterpaw 0 % , Scorching Elemental 0 %\n8 Heavy Armor Kit Olaf 0 %\nLogistics Task Briefing VII\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing VII","desc":"The Ironforge Brigade's supply of armor kits in the battlefield is running dangerously low. Obtain a batch and deliver them to Janela Stouthammer at the Ironforge Brigade's outpost outside Hive'Zora.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":32.9,"y":52.5,"n":"Janela Stouthammer","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8540":{"id":8540,"t":"Boots for the Guard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Ornate Mithril Boots to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing II in order to complete this quest.\n3 Ornate Mithril Boots\nLogistics Task Briefing II\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing II","desc":"The mounted division of the Cenarion Hold guard is in short supply of ornate mithril boots. Procure a batch and deliver them immediately to Captain Vish Kozus in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":33.7,"n":"Vish Kozus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"460":{"id":460,"t":"Resting in Pieces","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Alaric's Head to his grave.\nA Talking Head Rot Hide Bruiser 3 % , Raging Rot Hide 3 % , Rot Hide Savage 3 % , Rot Hide Plague Weaver 3 % and 1 more\nProvided: A Talking Head","desc":"You don't look like a rot hide. Good. I had lost hope...\nMy name is Alaric, and I was once Thule's head servant and bodyguard. He used his magic to \"protect\" me from the Plague of Undeath, but instead his spell gave me an unlife from which I cannot escape. And after creating the cursed rot hide gnolls, Thule beheaded me... and gave my head to the gnolls as a plaything!\nPlease, take me to my body. I believe the gnolls buried it here in Fenris Keep, near the stable, in an unmarked grave.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"This grave was hastily dug.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I had feared the Gnolls destroyed my body. It is good to know they did not.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":67.9,"y":24.9,"n":"Shallow Grave","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"79980":{"id":79980,"t":"Scramble","lv":24,"min":14,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find what awaits you.","desc":"\"Not so bad, eh? Since you're reading this, it means my stash is still there. Take a hundred paces due north and don't break your ankles going down the steep cliffside. There should be enough to keep you going.\"","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSilver Star Item 217314 Item 217315\nYou will also receive:\n200 Feathered Arrow 200 Exploding Shot Item 216619\nExperience: 200","done":"You pull a messenger bag out of the ground. Stuffed in with the supplies is a dirty parchment.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":40.8,"y":52.5,"n":"Pocket Litter","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":39.6,"y":49.9,"n":"Mound of Dirt","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"540":{"id":540,"t":"Preserving Knowledge","lv":38,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Recovered Tomes and the Worn Leather Book containing The Arm of Gri'lek to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.\n5 Recovered Tome Crushridge Plunderer 15 % , Crushridge Warmonger 15 % , Crushridge Enforcer 15 % , Crushridge Mage 15 % and 3 more\nWorn Leather Book Weathered Bookcase","desc":"Those beastly ogres now reside within Alterac's ruins, and I shudder to think what they're doing with the precious books still there. You must recover what you can!\nEnter the Ruins of Alterac and search for tomes looted by the ogres. Get whatever you can find and bring them to me, but also seek out one book in particular: The Arm of Gri'lek. It contains ancient troll lore that I must learn, and the Ruins of Alterac was the last known location of an intact copy of this book.","rew":"Experience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I wish I could search the ruins too, but I fear these bones wouldn't hold me during my climb up the mountains. However, how does your hunt for knowledge progress, ‹name›?","done":"Oh, you got them! Splendid! I must begin studying the Arm of Gri'lek immediately!\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"97420":{"id":97420,"t":"Reduce reuse reconcile","lv":36,"min":31,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Acquire 5 Drums of Crude Oil from the Venture Co. operations at Lake Nazferiti, then return to Knaz Blunderflame in Stranglethorn Vale.\n5 Drum of Crude Oil","desc":"I have a favor to ask of someone, and you look helpful!\nYou see this baby here? Ain't she a beaut? This is my newest racer, designed and built all by myself, because SOMEONE wouldn't help. I plan on taking this to the races in Thousand Needles, but it needs a little extra kick.\nNow, I'm too handsome to be a goblin, and I know better than to trust their tech, but I know the Venture Co struck liquid gold over at the lake. I'm sure they won't mind if you, erm, borrowed some? They won't even notice!","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\nStranglethorn Vale Open the zone on the world map Level 36 , requires level 31 Difficulty 31 32 34 39 46 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 97420","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"620":{"id":620,"t":"The monogrammed sash","lv":50,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return the Monogrammed Sash to its owner.\nProvided: Monogrammed Sash","desc":"This fine sash has the letters \"HS\" embroidered along its hem.\nLevel 50 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 46 48 53 60 Side Both factions Quest ID 620","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8060":{"id":8060,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Illusionist's Wraps","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing Primal Hakkari Bindings. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Bindings\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Mages in our tribe are known as illusionists. They employ powerful mojo in their incantations, often befuddling and confusing the tribe's enemies!\n<Al'tabim laughs wickedly.>\nIt is quite the sight to see a powerful illusionist at work, bringing our enemies to their knees from their own madness!\nFor you to know the way of our illusionists, go to Zul'Gurub and bring back to me selected Paragons of Power. For this, I will give you arm wraps our illusionists use to weave their spells.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Illusionist's Wraps\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"‹name› - you've returned already? Were you able to get the Paragons of Power I need?","done":"Impressive... could you feel the mojo flowing through them? The Paragons of Power were used as currency of sorts back when the Gurubashi Empire ruled these lands. Now we Zandalar will use the latent mojo inside of them to fight the second rise of the Blood God Hakkar!\nYou've done well today - consider yourself to have a friend in the Zandalar. For that, here are the illusionist's wraps I promised!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8620":{"id":8620,"t":"The Only Prescription","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover the 8 lost chapters of Draconic for Dummies and combine them with the Magical Book Binding and return the completed book of Draconic for Dummies: Volume II to Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris.\nDraconic For Dummies: Volume II\nProvided: Magical Book Binding","desc":"I should have known. My arch-enemy, Doctor Weavil, up to his old tricks! And now, thanks to your failure in Winterspring, Doctor Weavil has destroyed my book! How are you going to save the world now, hero?\nThe note I received stated that the only known copy of \"Draconic for Dummies: Volume II\" was ripped into 8 parts and scattered to the wind! If you somehow manage to find those missing chapters, use this magical binding to put them back together and return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nGnomish Turban of Psychic Might\nExperience: 6,600\n+75 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"I put my pants on just like you - one leg at a time. Except when my pants are on, I make arcanite buoys. Arcanite buoys, baby!","done":"Fantastic! I can't believe you went through the hassle! Are you some kind of machine? If it were me, I would have probably just let the world implode.\nI tip my turban to you, sir. And no good deed should go unrewarded.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"940":{"id":940,"t":"Teldrassil","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 440 experience instead of 230, 1.91 times as much. New rewards: Forest Oracle's Cloak.","obj":"Deliver the Inscribed Bark to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\nInscribed Bark\nProvided: Inscribed Bark","desc":"The forest whispers of your feats of valor, ‹name›. As I felt the harpies forced from their nests, a greater calm spread across the forest, its creatures once again feeling safe. I have feared sending another messenger to the Arch Druid, but I know that you will see my message safely to him.\nDeliver this to him and know that the forest will see you safely along its paths to the forest of stone.","rew":"New in Forever: Forest Oracle's Cloak.\nYou will receive:\nForest Oracle's Cloak\nExperience: 440\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hmm... You come with the spirit of the forest strongly within you, ‹class›. What business do you have with the Arch Druid of the Kaldorei?","done":"I wondered why the Oracle Tree had not communicated with me for so long... It seems that some problems are lessened while others grow to greater concerns.\nI fear my work on Teldrassil shall never be completed, and our immortality never restored.\nNonetheless, you have done the Oracle Tree's task well, and should be rewarded for your diligence.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":38.2,"y":34.4,"n":"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37,"y":34.1,"n":"Oracle Tree Bark","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":8.8,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"860":{"id":860,"t":"Sergra Darkthorn","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 85 experience instead of 90, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.","desc":"If you wish to walk the hunter's path, then your journey leads to the Barrens. Its beasts are strong-willed and fierce. You will learn much by hunting there, and your spirit will grow.\nSpeak with Sergra Darkthorn. She will be your first guide in the Barrens.\nSergra is at the Crossroads. To reach her, travel east from Bloodhoof Village into the Barrens, then north as the road forks. And have care as you travel--the Barrens holds great danger for the unprepared and unwary.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"You want to hunt in the Barrens?\nYour eyes are eager, and young. They're not yet squinted from tracking your prey across this land's dry plains.\nBut worry not. We'll toughen your body and your mind. And we'll teach you that there is more to hunting than finding and killing your quarry.\nPrepare yourself. Your journey begins. Now.\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":61.5,"y":80.9,"n":"Melor Stonehoof","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1100":{"id":1100,"t":"Lonebrow's Journal","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read Henrig Lonebrow's Journal.\nLonebrow's Journal\nProvided: Lonebrow's Journal","desc":"You slowly open the weathered journal of Henrig Lonebrow....","rew":"Experience: 1,350","back":"From your look of concern, I can tell that something is amiss....","done":"You say you found this journal on a deceased dwarf? Give me but a moment to peruse the pages...\nThousand Needles Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":30.7,"y":24.3,"n":"Henrig Lonebrow's Journal","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":89.6,"y":46.6,"n":"Falfindel Waywarder","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1180":{"id":1180,"t":"Goblin Sponsorship","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay.","desc":"Back to what you came here about. I know I promised Pozzik that I'd deliver a new fuel regulator for him, but I still haven't received it yet. Revilgaz over in Booty Bay said he'd have it shipped over, but it might be it slipped through the cracks somehow.\nIf that's true, there's not much we can do about it. We can at least find out if it was dispatched from Booty Bay.\nCheck in with Wharfmaster Lozgil over there, he should be able to check the cargo records.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Ratchet\n+25 reputation with Booty Bay\n-125 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Shipments to Ratchet? Let me just check the logbooks...\nNo, the most recent shipment I have on record of going out to Ratchet were boots from Drizzlik. Hasn't been much else, other than building supplies and tools. Definitely no race parts.\nThe Barrens Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.3,"y":73.6,"n":"Wharfmaster Lozgil","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7820":{"id":7820,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Thunder Bluff for your generous actions. Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":43,"y":42.7,"n":"Rumstag Proudstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"380":{"id":380,"t":"Night Web's Hollow","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Executor Arren wants you to kill 10 Young Night Web Spiders and 8 Night Web Spiders.\nYoung Night Web Spider slain : 0/ 10\nNight Web Spider slain : 0/ 8","desc":"One of our greatest struggles is obtaining the natural resources we need to survive. Gold was scarce even in the height of the Alliance's power.\nThere is a gold mine to the northwest that has been overrun with spiders. We need gold from the mine, but we can't very well get it while the spiders are crawling around in there. I've not much manpower to commit to the task, so we'll just have to do it little by little.\nGet up there and see what you can do for us, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlax Vest Rugged Mail Vest Zombie Skin Leggings\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Be wary of the spiders' venom, ‹name›. If you feel a sharp burning, you may want to have it looked at.","done":"Hmm, well, it's a start. It'll take a few weeks or months to fully clean out the infestation. After that, we'll have to get down there with some torches to burn away the webbing.\nYou've done your duty well, ‹name›, I'm sure I can find something else for you to do.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.2,"y":66,"n":"Executor Arren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1500":{"id":1500,"t":"Waking naralex","lv":25,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Level 25 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 21 23 28 33 Side Both factions Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 1500","cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"1740":{"id":1740,"t":"The Orb of Soran'ruk","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,100 experience instead of 2,550, 2 times as much. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Find 3 Soran'ruk Fragments and 1 Large Soran'ruk Fragment and return them to Doan Karhan in the Barrens.\n3 Soran'ruk Fragment Twilight Acolyte\nLarge Soran'ruk Fragment Shadowfang Darksoul in Shadowfang Keep","desc":"When demons of the Legion fall out of favor, their spirits are imprisoned within orbs and distributed to their mages and warlocks.\nMany were carried by their servants in Azeroth. Even fragmented, they still possess the powers of the demons trapped inside.\nThe orb of Soran'ruk was broken into two pieces, one was further broken to be used by the acolytes of the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. The other, larger piece, was possessed by a wizard in Shadowfang Keep. Find them and I can reform it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOrb of Soran'ruk Staff of Soran'ruk\nExperience: 5,100","back":"It took me many years to collect the pieces of the orb of Zargain, but it has served me well, as I am sure the orb of Soran'ruk will serve you.","done":"Yes... The orb was not greatly fragmented, and almost all of the pieces are here. It is a simple thing to recreate them, to make Soran'ruk whole again.\nI have dedicated my life to the study of the Burning Legion's orbs and their recreation. You have done me a favor collecting these pieces to study, and I will give you them back - fully reconstructed - in a form of your choosing.\nThe Barrens Ashenvale Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.3,"y":57.2,"n":"Doan Karhan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"3100":{"id":3100,"t":"Simple Letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Letter and speak to Llane Beshere in Northshire Abbey.\nSimple Letter\nProvided: Simple Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Llane, our local warrior trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, you got my letter, ‹name›... good.\nThere's been an influx of warriors in Elwynn recently - which is good for Stormwind, but bad for the kobolds and Defias in the area.","done":"Get yourself squared away, learn the layout of the land, and come back to me whenever you need training. I'll be here night or day.\nThe Knights of the Silver Hand have done well in making this place fairly safe, but as you meet the other citizens, I think you'll find they all have problems they could use some help with--help a warrior can give them. Good luck.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":50.2,"y":42.3,"n":"Llane Beshere","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1820":{"id":1820,"t":"Speak with Coleman","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Coleman Farthing.","desc":"You have proven your value to the Dark Lady, now perhaps you can prove yourself to one of her subjects.\nColeman Farthing awaits a warrior who is willing to be his instrument of revenge against the Forsaken's enemies.\nYou will find him in the Gallow's End Tavern in eastern Brill.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"Yes, it is true. I have need for your skills in combat. My means are small, but my task aids both me and the Forsaken's cause. Do it, and your reward will be twofold.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":58.2,"y":51.4,"n":"Deathguard Dillinger","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52.3,"n":"Coleman Farthing","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"140":{"id":140,"t":"Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Captain Sander's Locker. No longer rewards Captain Sander's Booty Bag.","obj":"Locate Captain Sanders' chest and open it for your reward.\nProvided: Final Clue to Sander's Treasure","desc":"Sure enough, deep within the Old Jug there is another clue to Sander's treasure. The ink has run in some places and the paper smells like whiskey but you can make out some of the text: Now that ye found me ol' whiskey jug, you're almost to the treasure! Just face West from the bottle and walk down to the shore. Once ye get to the water, keep going! Swim straight west till you find the island with me treasure chest!","rew":"New in Forever: Captain Sander's Locker.\nYou will receive:\nSilver Bar Captain Sander's Shirt Captain Sander's Sash Captain Sander's Locker\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150","done":"The hinges on the old chest are rusty but they still work. You force the chest open and take the booty.\nCongratulations!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":40.6,"y":17,"n":"Old Jug","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":26,"y":16.9,"n":"Locked Chest","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92460":{"id":92460,"t":"Coming of age","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.","desc":"Look at you, bright eyed and ready for adventure! We've been awaiting your arrival and anticipating your much needed help here in Thendal Village. I imagine you are brimming with both nerves and excitement for what is to come. After all, you only get to come of age once in a lifetime.\n<Ailee smiles kindly.>\nGo, seek out our village leader Rorian the Dayseeker at the entrance to the greatfather tree just west of here. He will get you started on your journey.","rew":"You will receive:\nAncient Heirloom\nExperience: 40\n+25 reputation with Windshapers\n+25 reputation with High Order","done":"Gale's greetings, Unwanted. I am honored to bestow your coming of age relic today as you are recognized for the potential you bring to the shen'dorei. Our people have faced great hardship and persecution in our complex history.\nToday you are given this relic which is one of many held by those before you. Someday when your ashes are scattered to the winds it will pass to another to continue our tradition.\nAs you take this relic with you know that the winds of home will be with you wherever you travel.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.8,"y":23.4,"n":"Ailee Farheart","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92700":{"id":92700,"t":"The grand skyseer","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.","desc":"Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the Windshapers here. The current Grand Skyseer and her people operate out of the lodge near the center of Valanaar.\nYou should also be aware, the Windshapers and High Order don't get along very well in these parts. Be careful and give the High Order a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar.","done":"Elder Amberwind sent me a message about you and your exploits in Shen'dar Village. You are most welcome here, friend.\nYou have a strong aura, and you clearly have a resonance with the spirits. Fewer and fewer of us have the skysight of late, and Zephras needs those with the gift if we are to survive these trying times. I am glad you have found your way to me.\nI look forward to further making your acquaintance.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"99260":{"id":99260,"t":"Fillions mission","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar.","desc":"I was tasked to retrieve important data on the flow of elemental energy from the Overlook Standing Stones. That data is vital to our plans to safely travel between Skywall and Azeroth. Without that data to aid in our calculations, our attempts to steer our skycutter ships through the elemental plane will fail.\nThe data is likely lost at this point, and I'm in no state to attempt to gather it again. I told the Supreme Magister of your role in saving me, and he wishes to speak with you again.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":79.8,"n":"Fillion Flamebreeze","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93740":{"id":93740,"t":"Blood for blood","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charms from the corpses of Al'Aketh cultists in the Gustberry Lowlands.\n10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charm","desc":"A number of our Windshaper novices were found dead in the Highlands this morning. We can't be certain but there is a strong chance that the Al'Aketh are responsible. Windshapers trade blood for blood, every time.\nHead north and kill any Al'Aketh you encounter. Bring me their windstone prayer charms as proof of the deed. We do not forgive and we do not forget.","back":"The Al'Aketh have engaged in their bloody zealotry for far too long. This is only the start of the reckoning they face.","done":"<Ayessa looks shaken and distant as you hand her the windstone charms.>\nDon't mind me, Sladkiy. Today has merely been... a trying day. Thank you for your service to the windshapers thus far.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92860":{"id":92860,"t":"In service of zephras","lv":12,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Valennia Stormfist and let her know that High Order is with them in their fight against the Al'Aketh.","desc":"The High Order has done our best to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but that is clearly no longer an option. Their hostility has been clearly demonstrated, and now there's rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island. They are clearly gearing up for something and whatever it is can't be good for the people of Zephras.\nReport to Valennia Stormfist and inform her that the High Order offers our full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise.","done":"I am sorry to hear about Belathaan. He was actually my cousin and he was a good mage and servant of Zephras. We will avenge him.\nYou seem eager to lend aid immediately. Come, let's speak further on the current situation.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});